From 18f4add731419a03dc52671aabf721fb0799b51a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai-Heng Feng <kai.heng.feng@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 30 May 2024 16:52:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 064/468] BACKPORT: FROMLIST: PCI: vmd: Let OS control ASPM for
 devices under VMD domain

Intel SoC cannot reach lower power states when mapped VMD PCIe bridges
and NVMe devices don't have ASPM configured.

So set aspm_os_control attribute to let OS really enable ASPM for those
devices.

Fixes: f492edb40b54 ("PCI: vmd: Add quirk to configure PCIe ASPM and LTR")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-pm/218aa81f-9c6-5929-578d-8dc15f83dd48@panix.com/
Signed-off-by: Kai-Heng Feng <kai.heng.feng@canonical.com>

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20240530085227.91168-2-kai.heng.feng@canonical.com
[ Kimi Code: on reapplication to v7.3-rc1, upstream moved
   pci_enable_link_state_locked() from the posting's anchor to the
   end of vmd_pm_enable_quirk(); the aspm_os_control assignment was
   kept at the function top so it still precedes the link-state
   enable. Content identical to the posting. ]
Signed-off-by: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/vmd.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/vmd.c b/drivers/pci/controller/vmd.c
index 9d97a832785ee..bdc94807617a0 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/vmd.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/vmd.c
@@ -922,6 +922,8 @@ static int vmd_pm_enable_quirk(struct pci_dev *pdev, void *userdata)
 	if (!(features & VMD_FEAT_BIOS_PM_QUIRK))
 		return 0;
 
+	pdev->aspm_os_control = 1;
+
 	pos = pci_find_ext_capability(pdev, PCI_EXT_CAP_ID_LTR);
 	if (!pos)
 		goto out_state_change;
-- 
